-### [Direct Voxel Grid Optimization](4694-direct-voxel-grid-optimization.md)
-Direct Voxel Grid Optimization (DVG) reconstructs per-scene radiance fields from calibrated images by directly optimizing a dense 3D voxel grid for density and a feature voxel grid for color, achieving convergence in less than 15 minutes on a single GPU. Unlike [Neural Radiance Fields](4972-neural-radiance-fields.md) which uses an implicit MLP, DVG uses explicit discretized volumes, and unlike prior voxel methods that convert from trained implicit models, it trains the voxel grid directly from scratch without cross-scene pretraining. It distinguishes itself from siblings like [Point-NeRF](6569-point-nerf.md) by using a dense grid with post-activation interpolation to produce sharp surfaces at lower resolutions, and from [MVSNeRF](6628-volume-feature-rendering.md) by achieving higher PSNR without requiring generalizable pre-training.
 
